id: pm-ado-1zuu
title: Map typed work item relations onto pm parent and dependency kinds in both directions
description: "Azure DevOps relations are typed rather than free-form: Parent, Child, Related, Duplicate, Predecessor and Successor each carry meaning the pm model already has a home for. Parent and Child map onto pm hierarchy, and the remaining kinds map onto pm dependency kinds. Round-tripping them preserves structure that a flat field-only sync would discard, and it is what lets a project imported from Azure DevOps still answer a pm graph query."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: "area:mapping",breaking
created_at: "2026-09-02T18:06:05.839Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T20:14:50.082Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: Each relation kind round-trips without loss; a cycle introduced remotely is refused rather than written into the local hierarchy; an unmapped relation kind is reported rather than silently dropped
parent: pm-ado-g4v1
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-12T23:06:33.094Z",pi-agent,"Audit 2026-09-13: EXISTS — mapRelations (index.ts line 506) maps all six ADO relation kinds to pm kinds via RELATION_MAP (parent, child, related, duplicate, blocked_by, blocks); unmapped relation kinds are reported in the unmapped array rather than silently dropped, tested in test/ado.test.ts. REMAINS — only the ADO-to-pm read direction is implemented; there is no pm-to-ADO reverse mapping for writes (buildUpdatePatch handles fields only, not relations), so relations do not round-trip. No cycle detection or refusal exists: a cycle introduced remotely would be written into the local hierarchy without refusal. Both missing pieces are required by the acceptance criteria."
  "2026-10-07T19:56:33.099Z",codex-sol,"Baseline acceptance against the built dist/index.js with a real scratch pm project: persisted parent plus related dependency successfully; mapRelations returns two links for a repeated relation; buildUpdatePatch emits only test /rev for an empty field set; no relation import/export functions exist. Acceptance scenario: fixture batch reads containing reciprocal hierarchy, predecessor/successor, Related, Duplicate and configured custom types import to real pm links, export via revision-checked relation patches, and repeat with zero duplicate links or writes. Unknown types and missing targets must be reported and retained remotely; remote cycles and conflicting parents must fail before local writes. Design uses a caller-owned real PmClient, preserving the extension runtime type-only SDK boundary."
  "2026-10-07T20:04:40.888Z",codex-sol,"Implemented additive import and minimal export plans using a caller-owned SDK client, full-corpus reads, exact source_kind provenance, reciprocal endpoints and pre-write hierarchy validation. Real SDK probe found no accepted duplicate dependency kind even with extension registration; Duplicate is preserved as related plus its exact forward/reverse reference in source_kind. Distinct same-target Related/Duplicate/custom dependencies persist independently. Full project sync and deletion reconciliation remain separate API orchestration work. No remote service or credentials used."
  "2026-10-07T20:08:16.718Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: built successfully with deduplication removed from mapRelations; duplicate-mapping test failed on 2 links versus 1. Built with exportRelations returning an empty relation plan (previous field-only behavior); stale/duplicate-export test failed on missing removals at indices 3, 2, 1. Built with only importRelations cycle preflight disabled; disconnected-cycle test failed because one SDK parent write entered history before the SDK rejected the eventual cycle. All exports and test imports remained intact. Restored implementation passed the combined three-test pattern. Raised peer and manifest minimum to the tested SDK 2026.10.4 complete-list/provenance contract; included typed-relation documentation in the packed distribution."
  "2026-10-07T20:14:49.395Z",codex-sol,"Validation passed: linked source/built behavioral suite 47/47 with zero skips; npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 139/139 with zero skips, 100% measured Node V8 lines/branches/functions across all four configured source files, docstrings 40/40 across seven scanned files, zero production audit vulnerabilities, pack dry-run, changelog check, publish-attestation and version-derived changelog-date checks. The existing statement-metric enforcement gap remains tracked by pm-ado-5w3m. Packed npm/Node and Bun consumers passed real-tracker hierarchy/provenance/re-sync/revision-patch/doc-presence acceptance. Every remote call used HTTP fixtures. Import merges additively; whole-project sync, deletion reconciliation and multi-item transactionality are explicit boundaries. Duplicate semantics remain related plus exact source_kind because of the SDK enum gap; no SDK issue filed. Package releases remain gated and were neither enabled nor run."
